      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hmm... so, in legacy mode we do care to put the iommu domain, but in scalable mode we don\u0027t even check if there are any domains still associated with any PASID entries behind this context entry?\n\n...Question: when this hypercall is called in scalable mode, are there still any domains associated with PASID entries behind this context entry? IOW, does the host call pkvm_hc_iommu_clear_pasid_entry() for all those PASID entries before calling pkvm_hc_iommu_clear_ce() for this context entry, or not? (I suppose it doesn\u0027t.)",
      "revId": "78c41d21f5e4117220a790e69f08e5af1a51c0c3",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "379fbab8_dbc3bfb0",
        "filename": "arch/x86/kvm/vmx/pkvm/hyp/pv_iommu.c",
        "patchSetId": 84
      },
      "lineNbr": 175,
      "author": {
        "id": 3702829
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-12-12T00:34:57Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If I understand correctly, the iommu subsystem considers it okay to have the context cleared before pasid entries are cleared. During a hot-unplug scenario, i think the context gets cleared first during device cleanup, but PASIDs attached to processes or VMS will be cleared later only.\n\nThis was my understanding and from the code I could not see a device removal code path or iommu group removal code path(both does SM context clear) directly trying to remove pasid entries. Pasid entry gets cleared when a device gets detached from domain or a process or VM unbinds a device.",
      "parentUuid": "7753e1c9_a78303dd",
      "revId": "78c41d21f5e4117220a790e69f08e5af1a51c0c3",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "a2619124_01f9f478",
        "filename": "arch/x86/kvm/vmx/pkvm/hyp/pv_iommu.c",
        "patchSetId": 84
      },
      "lineNbr": 175,
      "author": {
        "id": 2022314
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-12-12T01:03:02Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "So, the host clears the context entry without bothering to clear its child PASID entries, and that in itself is fine (no need to clear them, just need to free them), but for us (for pKVM) it means that the host will never issue the clear_pasid_entry hypercall for those PASID entries, thus we will never decrease the refcount of their corresponding IOMMU domains.\n\nSo we have a resource leak, and a potential functionality issue: the host will try to free an IOMMU domain later, and will fail, since pKVM will return an error, since the domain\u0027s refcount is \u003e1?\n\nSo it seems like we should put the iommu domains in pkvm_pasid_free_table()?",
      "parentUuid": "7753e1c9_a78303dd",
      "revId": "78c41d21f5e4117220a790e69f08e5af1a51c0c3",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "2ca17bf3_0c732d93",
        "filename": "arch/x86/kvm/vmx/pkvm/hyp/pv_iommu.c",
        "patchSetId": 84
      },
      "lineNbr": 175,
      "author": {
        "id": 3702829
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-12-12T01:14:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think the host will issue clear_pasid_entry when the process or device is unbound and the domain will be freed only after all the attached pasid entries are unbound. From my understanding, domain free is not dependent on SM context entry clear, but the attached PASIDs \n\nI am unable to test this with pKVM as we do not support device assignment. In the normal case we attach the device with IOMMU_NO_PASID and we have verified that the domain gets freed as expected when we detach the domain(dma to identity).",
      "parentUuid": "a2619124_01f9f478",
      "revId": "78c41d21f5e4117220a790e69f08e5af1a51c0c3",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
